    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0413" n="281" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515PC/347: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Arica</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Von Tresckow</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Arica</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-01-18T18:00:00-04:42"><hi rendition="#italic">January 18,
                                1926—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 19—12:35
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>From Pershing.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>With reference to my contemplated absence from Arica and from duty in
                        connection with the Plebiscitary Commission, Tacna-Arica Arbitration on
                        account of illness and further reference to Arbitrator’s ruling that no one
                        can be designated as commissioner ad interim, I hereby tender my resignation
                        as commissioner in order that an American member may be appointed in my
                        place.</item>
                    <pb facs="0414" n="282" xml:id="pg282"/>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>I consider it important that the president of the Commission be here in
                        the territory or near at hand at all times and therefore recommend that my
                        resignation be accepted to take effect upon my departure from Arica and that
                        General Lassiter be appointed to take effect at the same time.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>General Lassiter is expected to arrive on the 21st and I shall leave as
                        soon thereafter as practicable and shall notify you the exact date when
                            determined.<anchor n="91" xml:id="d150-f1"/></item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Von Tresckow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d150-f1" n="91" xml:id="d150-f1-content">
                <p>General Pershing left Arica Jan. 27, 1926.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
